note: schema.q:18:1 — N_NO_HORIZON: table reactions: `sync to members[.$message.conversation]` has no horizon, so every row of every group a device holds reaches it and stays; a device that holds many groups, or a public table that grows, pays for all of it at every cold start; `cap 50 by message` bounds the rows per message, not what a device acquires — `sync to members[.$message.conversation]` delivers every message's rows to every device; measure what it costs with `check --residency`
